---
title: "Parse a command and report its outcome once"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: success
    lg1: active
    lg2: Breaks HooksRequireParsedAction
    lg3: Path to the HooksRequireParsedAction bug
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 breaks
  class lg3 bugPath
  s0: Parse argv and identify registration
  s1: Start the selected command
  s2: Record command invoked
  s3: Record command invoked (hooks ran without a parsed action)
  s4: Validate login and run the handler or help
  s5: Validate login and run the handler or help (hooks ran without a parsed action)
  s6: Record success or failure
  s7: Record success or failure (hooks ran without a parsed action)
  s8: Print only an unreported failure
  s9: Print only an unreported failure (hooks ran without a parsed action)
  s10: Preserve exit markers for the runner
  s11: Preserve exit markers for the runner (hooks ran without a parsed action)
  s12: Invocation ended
  s13: Invocation ended (hooks ran without a parsed action)
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: effect/cli selects a registration or effect/cli prints the parse error and names its command
  s1 --> s2: run enabled hooks for parsed input
  s1 --> s3: run enabled hooks for parsed input
  s2 --> s4: record invoked after hooks
  s3 --> s5: record invoked after hooks
  s4 --> s6: handler or help succeeds or handler fails before printing or parser or handler already reports the failure
  s5 --> s7: handler or help succeeds or keep the parse failure already printed by effect/cli
  s6 --> s8: record the same command outcome
  s7 --> s9: record the same command outcome
  s8 --> s10: nothing remains to print or print failure and preserve its cause
  s9 --> s11: nothing remains to print
  s10 --> s12: runner uses the marked outcome
  s11 --> s13: runner uses the marked outcome
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
